---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
const pageSlug = 'features-encryption';
const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'AES-256 encryption on device',
  description: 'How Vireault uses Argon2id, AES-256-GCM, a random master key and an encrypted index on Android.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vireault' },
  datePublished: '2026-11-05',
  dateModified: '2026-11-05',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://vireault.app/features/encryption',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AES-256 encryption on device"
  description="Vireault encrypts Android vault files with AES-256-GCM, derives keys with Argon2id, and keeps an encrypted index with hidden file names."
  path="/features/encryption"
  pageSlug={pageSlug}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={articleLd}
  article={{ published: '2026-11-05', modified: '2026-11-05' }}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/features', label: 'Features' }, { label: 'Encryption' }]} />
    <article class="section prose">
      <h1>AES-256 encryption on your Android phone</h1>
      <p>Vireault is built around on-device cryptography. Content is not “hidden” by renaming a folder or changing an icon. Files are encrypted before they rest in the vault.</p>
      <h2>What ships today</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Argon2id</strong> key derivation from your unlock secret</li>
        <li><strong>AES-256-GCM</strong> for vault file contents</li>
        <li>A <strong>random master key</strong> that wraps the encrypted data</li>
        <li>An <strong>encrypted index</strong> so file names stay hidden on disk</li>
      </ul>
      <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} heading="Encrypt a private album on Android" />
      <h2>Why the index matters</h2>
      <p>Even when file bytes are encrypted, cleartext names can leak what you stored. Vireault encrypts the index as well, which reduces that metadata leak on the device filesystem.</p>
      <h2>What encryption does not replace</h2>
      <p>If someone knows your PIN, pattern or passphrase, they can open the vault. Choose a strong secret, enable lockout discipline, and keep backup recovery material offline. Related reading: <a href="/features/unlock">unlock methods</a>, <a href="/features/offline">offline design</a>, and <a href="/guides/encrypt-files-on-android">encrypting files on Android</a>.</p>
      <h2>Honest boundaries</h2>
      <p>We do not claim third-party audits on this page. We describe the algorithms and local model the app uses. For privacy practices, see the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
